course: dictionary
lesson: 11443
title: Stick to it: adhere
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word adhere means to stick firmly to something. Think of glue, tape or a sticker pressed onto paper. When a sticker adheres to a page, it stays there and does not fall off.
explain: «The label will adhere to the jar if you press it hard.» The clue is press it hard. Pressing helps something stick, so adhere must mean stick firmly. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The label will stick firmly to the jar" still makes sense.
explain: Adhere can also mean to keep to a rule, plan or idea carefully. «Every pupil must adhere to the school rules.» Here nobody is gluing anything. Adhere means to follow the rules closely, without breaking them.
fact: Adhere is a verb, so its forms are adhere, adheres, adhered and adhering.
fact: «Adhere» means to stick firmly to something, like glue or tape.
fact: «Adhesive» is the name for sticky stuff, such as glue or sticky tape.
fact: «Adhere to» means to follow a rule, plan or belief carefully.
fact: Adhere is a formal word, so you will often meet it in school rules, instructions and science lessons.
exercise: «The label will adhere to the jar if you press it firmly.» What does adhere mean here? | To fall off quickly | To paint over | *To stick firmly to | To melt into water
exercise: «Every pupil must adhere to the school rules.» What does adhere to mean here? | To break the rules loudly | *To follow the rules carefully | To write new rules | To ignore the rules
exercise: Find and copy the word that names sticky stuff, such as glue. | sticker | paint | *adhesive | adhere
test: «Mia adhered to her plan and finished her reading before lunch.» Which word means about the same as adhered here? | Lost | Ripped | *Followed | Forgot
test: Which word is the name for sticky stuff, like glue or sticky tape? | Adhering | *Adhesive | Adheres | Adhered
exam: «The team adhered strictly to the plan, so every step was done in order.» What does adhered strictly to mean? | Lost the plan on the bus | Ignored the plan completely | Painted the plan a new colour | *Followed the plan very carefully
